Relationships Between Classes (OOP)

In Java, classes rarely exist alone. They work together by creating relationships.

There are mainly 5 relationships you should know:

    IS-A (Inheritance)
    HAS-A (Association)
    Aggregation
    Composition
    Dependency (USES-A)

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. IS-A Relationship (Inheritance)
    Definition

    One class becomes another class.

    Dog IS-A Animal
    Car IS-A Vehicle
    SavingsAccount IS-A BankAccount

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2. HAS-A Relationship (Association)

    A class contains another class as one of its members.

    Customer HAS-A Account

    Student HAS-A Laptop

    Employee HAS-A Address

    Customer
    -----------
    name
    age
    Account account

    HAS-A

    Account
    ---------
    accNo
    balance

    This is called Association. The two classes know each other.

    Real World Example

    Customer

    Name
    Email
    Phone

    ↓

    creates

    ↓

    Account

    Account Number
    Balance
    IFSC

    Customer object stores an Account object.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


Flow

    Login Screen

    ↓

    Validate Customer

    ↓

    Create Customer Object

    ↓

    Create Account Object

    ↓

    Link Customer with Account

    ↓

    Store both inside Database

Customer

    Customer customer = new Customer(...);

Account

    Account account = new Account(...);

Link

    customer.setAccount(account);

Now

    Customer HAS-A Account


There are two types.
HAS-A

    Aggregation
    Composition



---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3. Aggregation

    Definition

        A weak HAS-A relationship.

        The child object can exist independently.

        Example

            College HAS-A Students

            Department HAS-A Teachers

            Library HAS-A Books

        If

            College is deleted

            Students still exist.

            They can join another college.

        Example

            class Student{

            }

            class College{

                Student student;

            }

        Student can exist without College.Hence Aggregation.


        Characteristics

            Weak Relationship

            Independent Life Cycle

            Object Sharing Possible

        Example
            Person
            ↓

            owns

            ↓

            Car

            Even if

            Person object disappears,

            Car still exists.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. Composition

    A strong HAS-A relationship.

    Child object cannot exist without Parent.

    Example

        House HAS-A Room

        Car HAS-A Engine

        Human HAS-A Heart

        Destroy Car

        ↓

        Engine is also destroyed.

    Example

        class Engine{

        }

        class Car{

            private Engine engine =
                    new Engine();

        }

    Diagram



    Characteristics

        Strong Relationship

        Same Life Cycle

        Cannot exist separately

    Example
        Book contains Pages

            Delete Book

                 ↓

        Pages don't exist independently.


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

